  "limits": [
    "The ownership and queue graphs share branch choices from the same control-flow join. This is bounded relational proof coverage, not arbitrary predicate equivalence, dynamic owner unions or a new permission rule.",
    "Use checks read current facts, including intervening consuming calls and scope release. A registration snapshot cannot revive an invalidated owner. Unconditional use cannot rely on an acquisition that occurs only on some incoming paths. A supplemental native CoD run confirms an independent default-parameter bits copy remains valid after its source region is consumed.",
    "The native harness injects a failed registration in the acquisition branch. Its10000-iteration stress conditionally acquires5000 regions and drains one action per acquired instance; the phase asserts peak1 record. The complete fixture peaks at3 records/96bytes, and every record, callable image and region releases exactly once.",
    "The scale probe creates4/8/16/32/64 distinct conditional acquisitions and registrations. Temporary profiling identified repeated queue/fact walks across incoming completions; query-local sharing preserves the proof semantics without caching across compilation phases. Source hashes and emitted artifact sizes match before/after; prior textual artifacts were not retained for bytewise comparison. Timings are individual observations, not general complexity guarantees.",
    "Generated LLVM and native runtime C++ are both ASAN-instrumented. The scale measurement is frontend compilation; native process and link timings are reported separately.",
    "The owning deferred-call and delayed owning-block probes still reject at explicit implementation guards. H370 invocation-time transfer remains required work. Other unfinished work includes non-queryable provenance, broader predicate/target/result relations, mutable ownership backedges, generic capture transport, module queues and broader callable-family/AOT composition.",
    "D01 allocation/relocation, actual-owner unions, abstract-result ABI, D16 fractions, D22 construction choices and pure/TCO/compiler-pilot deferral retain their existing boundaries. No runtime storage or source-policy change is introduced."
  ]
